.DS_Store

# Generated 3D assets.
#
# assets/tripo holds the source of record and is committed: generation and
# rigging are both non-deterministic, so a lost GLB cannot be re-made from its
# prompt, and each one costs credits.
#
# public/tripo is the serving copy. The rigged fighters are committed and the
# rest is not: Vite copies public/ into the build without bundling it, so a
# rigged model costs a visitor nothing until the HD cast toggle actually asks
# for one — but without them in the repo that toggle does nothing on the
# deployed site. The unrigged fighters and the ammo props are dev-harness
# inputs only and would be dead weight in a deploy.
#
# Rebuild the serving copies with: node scripts/glb-optimise.mjs --all
assets/tripo/*.task.json
assets/tripo/*.rejected
public/tripo/*
!public/tripo/*-rigged.glb
!public/tripo/ammo-coconut.glb
!public/tripo/ammo-melon.glb
!public/tripo/ammo-cluster.glb
!public/tripo/ammo-hive.glb
!public/tripo/prop-*.glb
